    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The DSP method starts by drafting informal proofs for a given mathematical problem. These proofs are then mapped to formal proof sketches using a large language model. The formal proof sketches are <strong>partial proofs that outline high-level conjecture statements</strong>. The automated prover is used to fill in the gaps between the intermediate conjectures, resulting in a complete formal proof.",
